      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day by prescription (1,200 mg/day over the counter). A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 3,200 mg/day, the maximum, and is sometimes used for inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily.** This is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg by mouth every 4\u20136 hours as needed.** This is for pain or fever.\n\nIf 1600 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, I can enter 400 mg four times daily. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you meant 1600 mg per day or a single 1600 mg dose, let me know and we can sort out the right regimen."
      }
